    research: [
      { t: 'Lock scope to one thing: monocular pose estimation for R2 → R1 docking. R1 row-advance is explicitly out of scope.' },
      { t: 'Write the research question and hypothesis in one paragraph each: how model size and compute budget trade against docking reliability.' },
      { t: 'Define the four metrics now, before any code: translation/rotation error at dock, inference latency, peak memory, docking success rate.' },
      { t: 'Agent-assisted literature sweep (~15 papers): fiducial markers vs learned keypoints, lightweight backbones, space lighting and specular panels. Verify every citation actually exists.' },
      { t: 'Create the research repo: pinned requirements, seeded runs, README that states the question, data/ and results/ separated.' },
      { t: 'Decision memo: simulator choice (PyBullet vs Gazebo+ROS 2 vs Isaac) with the reason and the cost of being wrong.' },
